// What the Ash Remembers [B] (bible 4.3, 8.3): Aldermere asked the Unwriters to let it go. Wren arrives on its last
// day. Attend it to the end, or try to stop it and the Choir sings over the square (boss 6.6).
// Aldermere_2, the square. Mayor Hollin, a thrush, speaks for the village; Teodor stands at the edge.
// After (verdance-arc.md §1): Teodor leaves the square either way. Attended, the lane and the square are empty and
// the village stands as paper in the ash field (Aldermere_3), where Teodor sits with them (Aldermere_Ash_Teodor).
// Stopped, the Choir answered, Aldermere is still here with half a song (Aldermere_Hollin).

title: Aldermere_Teodor
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.aldermere.attended")>>
    Teodor: The square is paper now. They are in the Blank, cartographer. They asked for that. They are well. #still #face:grave #line:03bf87a
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("verdance.aldermere.stopped")>>
    <<jump Aldermere_Hollin>>
<<endif>>
Hollin: Welcome to Aldermere. There is bread. There is always bread on the last day. #face:bright #line:067ff9b
Hollin: We voted. Every hand. The Guild wanted four hundred crowns a street, and then we would be the same forever. #line:0dc835b
Hollin: We would rather be remembered than kept. The brothers were kind enough to ask us twice. #face:bright #line:0af2746
Teodor: Three times. I asked three times. I made sure. #face:grave #line:01bb513
-> Then I'll stay to the end. #line:0927bd2
    <<voice drift verdance>>
    <<jump Aldermere_Attend>>
-> I won't let you fade. #line:0bdd5a3
    <<voice warden verdance>>
    <<jump Aldermere_Stop>>
-> Who will remember you? #line:03aa299
    <<voice surveyor verdance>>
    Hollin: You will. That is why we are glad you came. A visitor is the best kind of memory. #face:bright #line:01796f6
    <<jump Aldermere_Attend>>
===

title: Aldermere_Attend
---
Hollin: Stay by the bread. The bells start at dusk. It does not hurt. Brother Teodor has done this before. #line:098c7b0
Teodor: The kindest thing you will see, cartographer. I am glad it is you watching. #face:bright #line:027960b
Hollin: When you pass again, do not look for us. Look for the ash field. We will be in it. #face:grave #line:095ba84
<<release Verdance_Aldermere_1>>
<<release Verdance_Aldermere_2>>
<<release Verdance_Aldermere_3>>
<<flag verdance.aldermere.attended 1>>
<<flag verdance.aldermere.decided 1>>
===

title: Aldermere_Stop
---
Teodor: Ah. May I say a thing you will not like? They did not ask you. #face:wary #line:056adf3
Hollin: Please. Put the quill down. We voted. #face:wary #line:07e3080
-> Put the bells down, then. #line:086ca69
    <<voice warden verdance>>
    Teodor: The Choir will not. They sing what was asked of them. I will neither stop them nor help them. #face:grave #line:0aedf36
-> ... #line:035eb61
    <<voice drift verdance>>
    Teodor: Then you must answer the Choir. I am sorry. It is the one thing I am sorry for today. #face:grave #line:070896b
<<flag verdance.aldermere.stopped 1>>
<<flag verdance.aldermere.decided 2>>
===

title: Aldermere_Hollin
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.aldermere.stopped")>>
    <<if has_flag("boss.choir.defeated") and not has_flag("verdance.aldermere.after_heard")>>
        Hollin: The bells stopped halfway. They have never stopped halfway. Nobody knows how the song ends now. #face:grave #line:0eff68e
        Hollin: The bread went stale. We had not baked for a tomorrow. We are baking. #line:08594d0
        Hollin: Every hand voted, and here we all are. I had forgotten what an ordinary morning weighs. #face:grave #line:0059fe4
        <<flag verdance.aldermere.after_heard 1>>
        -> Vote again, then. #line:09f6fb7
            <<voice warden verdance>>
            Hollin: We will. Every hand. And you will not be asked to stand in the square for it. #face:wary #line:05a73cb
        -> What do you need? #line:05204a4
            <<voice surveyor verdance>>
            Hollin: Flour, and the rest of the song. Teodor will not sing it. He says it is not his. #line:03a9127
        -> ... #line:087f06a
            <<voice drift verdance>>
            Hollin: Yes. That is the sound the square makes now. Half a bell. #face:grave #line:059a099
        <<stop>>
    <<endif>>
    Hollin: You are the one who stopped it. Thank you, I suppose. We are still here. We are still here. #still #face:grave #line:085ae22
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<jump Aldermere_Teodor>>
===

title: Aldermere_Ash_Teodor
---
<<if not has_flag("verdance.aldermere.ash_sat")>>
    Teodor: Cartographer. Sit, if you like. I come at dusk. They are at the bread now. #line:0b452c5
    Teodor: Hollin cuts it too thick. She always does. Nobody says so. It is a festival. #face:bright #line:0e589c5
    Teodor: I do not see them, you understand. I know where they stand. That is enough to sit by. #line:061cc4f
    <<flag verdance.aldermere.ash_sat 1>>
    -> I'll sit with you. #line:0830aee
        <<voice drift verdance>>
        Teodor: Thank you. It is a quiet festival from here. It is still a festival. #face:bright #line:0ee0f08
    -> Do they know you come? #line:0faa2be
        <<voice surveyor verdance>>
        Teodor: I asked them once, to be sure. Hollin said bread. I took it as yes. #face:bright #line:0df3a71
    -> You could have kept them. #line:051f91c
        <<voice warden verdance>>
        Teodor: I could have. They asked me not to. I asked them three times, and made sure. #face:grave #line:009a8a7
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Teodor: The bunting is still up. Nobody will take it down. Nobody needs to. #still #line:0d2a40c
===
